  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nThe upper ridging is expected to strengthen over the southeast\ninto the middle of next week. The sunny skies and building upper \nlevel ridging will make for a very warm conditions with highs \nclimbing back into the mid 80s to around 90 degrees.\n\nAn upper level low and associated longwave trough axis makes some\nslight progress pushing east into the upper ridge over the area \ntowards the end of the week/weekend. However, over much of the \narea the surface and upper ridge remain stout. However, enough \nforcing aloft and moisture convergence does setup over much of \nTennessee to produce some precipitation over that area. Our \nsouthern middle Tennessee counties could see some low end \nprecipitation chances, but consistency is too low to include at \nthis time. Most guidance does push a dry cold front through the \narea Friday or Friday night. This will bring cooler weather to to \nthe area that is more seasonable into the weekend.",
